Z||000000||SibERThuG||09-26-2000||11:32 PM||||When my car hits a bump the front end skips like a flat rock on water. On the turns and handling, the front end sways. I have an 88' Formula and the sway bars are A-O.K. I had it looked at and my mechanic says it's bad control arm bushings and bearings on my front driver's side. (In the rain I slid drivers side front tire first into a curb at 15 M.P.H.) I wanted to ask the opinions of Fiero nutz. Are these my problems??? What else could it be?? Shocks are fine. What else is there to go wrong. Help is greatly appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||SloPonti||09-27-2000||12:02 AM||||your mechanic is correct! the name of this is bumpsteer! it is common with worn suspension and steering parts!<BR>hope this helps!<BR>Rob||||reg||1
